# Frontend architecture

- Prefer React Server Components. Add `"use client"` only at the smallest boundary that requires browser state, effects, event handlers, or browser-only APIs.
- Prefer platform features, React, and existing dependencies. Add a dependency only when it measurably reduces complexity and cannot be covered cleanly by what is already installed.
- Make performance a first-class requirement: minimize client JavaScript, prevent layout shift, optimize fonts and images, and keep critical rendering paths lean.
- Keep components semantic and focused. Do not add speculative abstractions, wrappers, configuration, or folders.
- Preserve Persian/RTL behavior across responsive breakpoints. Use logical CSS properties where practical.

